# State Management (Cubit)
- Cubit only — no BLoC event classes, no other state management solution
- states are sealed/freezed unions: Initial, Loading, Success(data), Error(failure) — never nullable-field guessing (e.g. no `isLoading + data + error` all on one mutable state unless freezed union is overkill for a trivial toggle)
- Cubits depend only on domain use cases/repositories, injected via get_it constructor injection — never on data sources or dio directly
- one Cubit per feature/screen scope; do not share a single Cubit across unrelated widgets
- no async work inside build(); trigger via Cubit methods from initState, route entry, or user interaction
- emit new immutable state objects — never mutate and re-emit the same instance
- dispose/close resources (streams, controllers) in the Cubit's close() override
